  "verbalization": "Duvelisib is implicated in the treatment of Neoplasm Of Mature B-cells through a series of indirect pathways, primarily via the use of Bendamustine and Copanlisib. The evidence suggests that Duvelisib, through its indication for Acute Lymphoblastic/lymphocytic Leukemia and Richter Syndrome, is linked to Bendamustine, which in turn is associated with Neoplasm Of Mature B-cells. Similarly, Duvelisib's indication for Follicular Lymphoma leads to Copanlisib, which also has an indication for Neoplasm Of Mature B-cells. This suggests a potential mechanism where Duvelisib may exert its effects through a shared pathway involving the use of related drugs that target similar molecular processes in B-cell malignancies. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of these drugs in the treatment of B-cell neoplasms, emphasizing the importance of targeting pathways that are common across different B-cell disorders. The evidence supports a relationship between Duvelisib and Neoplasm Of Mature B-cells through the use of related drugs, suggesting a possible mechanism of action that involves the modulation of B-cell signaling pathways.",
